---
/**
 * A stray bit: every so often a filled square glides across the page behind the
 * text, turning a few times at right angles on the way, with a fading trail. It
 * is placed on the page rather than the viewport, so a scroll carries it off
 * with the text around it.
 *
 * The layer clips, so a bit past the right or bottom edge never widens or
 * lengthens the page, and it is zero tall between trips. Only the lead is in the
 * markup: the script adds the trail, which is the same flight played again by
 * each follower, a few ms late and dimmer. Its look and timing are
 * `data/bit.json`, tuned with the dev-only lab. See `scripts/bit.ts`.
 */
---

<div data-bit-layer aria-hidden="true" class="layer">
  <span data-bit class="bit"></span>
</div>

<style>
  .layer {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 0;
    overflow: clip;
    /* Behind the page: the text and art paint over it, and the sticky nav, the
       one opaque surface, hides it. The black is the canvas, so it stays below. */
    z-index: -1;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  /* Size and colours come from data/bit.json, set on the layer by the script. */
  .bit {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: var(--bit-size);
    height: var(--bit-size);
    background-color: var(--bit-lead);
    visibility: hidden;
  }
  /* Followers are cloned from the lead, so they carry its scoping attribute. */
  .bit.trail {
    background-color: var(--bit-trail);
  }
  .layer[data-flying] .bit {
    visibility: visible;
  }
</style>

<script>
  import '@/scripts/bit'
</script>
